{%- comment -%}
  One nav link, with the active state computed correctly.

  NOTE: Liquid's `assign` cannot evaluate a comparison. Assigning the result of
  `x == y` does NOT produce a boolean — it produces something always-truthy, so
  every link ends up active. Active state must be decided inside a real if/elsif
  block, as below. (Careful: Liquid parses tag syntax even inside comments, so
  don't write tag delimiters in prose here.)

  Params: include.item (the nav entry), include.cur (page.url),
          include.class (extra classes), include.icon (true → render the icon).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign item = include.item -%}
{%- assign is_active = false -%}
{%- if item.url == '/' -%}
  {%- if include.cur == '/' -%}{%- assign is_active = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- elsif include.cur contains item.url -%}
  {%- assign is_active = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
<a href="{{ item.url | relative_url }}"
   class="{{ include.class }}{% if is_active %} is-active{% endif %}"
   {% if is_active %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
  {%- if include.icon %}{% include icon.liquid name=item.icon %}{% endif -%}
  <span>{{ item.name }}</span>
</a>
